        "text": "Personal contact is a crucial component of successful campaigning in New Hampshire.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "John McCain held numerous town meetings in New Hampshire, engaging directly with attendees.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "At these meetings, McCain spoke about his interests and then walked around to shake hands and make eye contact.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "While personal contact alone is insufficient, it is necessary for other campaign efforts to succeed.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "George H. W. Bush visited multiple breakfast locations in New Hampshire after losing in Iowa.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
