        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Public trust in leaders is enhanced when communication feels direct and personal.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Online discourse lacks real-time emotional cues that moderate aggressive behavior.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The decline of shared physical presence in dialogue contributes to sharper political discourse.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Social media amplifies polarization by enabling anonymous, unmoderated conflict.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Audiences value authenticity and relatability in presidential communication.",
