  {
    "episode_id": 64569,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64569.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, they ought to make a distinction in their head if they want to get involved, whether they want to get involved in public service in government versus getting involved in politics, going, seeking elected office. And they're really two different avenues of approach. But frankly, get yourself prepared in your profession, know what you're talking about, and then go do it. Because the circumstances of the moment will be much more important in dictating whether you succeed or not than any advice I can give you.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "There should be a clear mental distinction made between public service in government and pursuing political office.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Public service in government and seeking elected office represent two distinct approaches.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "It is essential to be well-prepared in one's profession before engaging in public involvement.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Having expertise in one's field is crucial when contributing to public affairs.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The current circumstances of the moment have greater influence on success than personal advice.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Success in public engagement depends significantly on external contextual factors rather than individual preparation alone.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker’s own advice is less valuable than real-world conditions in determining outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Audience members are likely to benefit from practical readiness over theoretical guidance.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Professional competence is a credible foundation for meaningful civic participation.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "People who seek public roles often conflate government service with electoral politics.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 64569,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64569.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "So let me probe this a little further as an engineer. I am one, I know that you are one as well. I'm curious as to whether or not you favor engineers over other disciplines who may be interested in politics or the other way around.",
